    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0028" n="24" xml:id="pg24"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.94/339: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-27T11:00:00+09:00">April 27, 1939—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 27—1:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>204. For Hornbeck. My letter April 12.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d24-f1"/> Prince
                        Chichibu<anchor n="27" xml:id="d24-f2"/> dined with us last night which gave
                    me a favorable opportunity to discuss with him the subject under reference. I
                    made full use of the opportunity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d24-f1" n="26" xml:id="d24-f1-content">
                <p>An attached notation by Frank Duvall, of the Office of the Adviser on Political
                    Relations, dated May 2, reads: “The letter of April 12, 1939, from Ambassador
                    Grew at Tokyo is regarding the possibility of Japan’s entering a military
                    alliance with Germany and Italy. Mr. Grew’s letter refers to a letter of
                    February 14, 1939, from Mr. Herschel Johnson at London to the Under Secretary on
                    the same subject.” Letters of April 12 and February 14, 1939, not found in
                    Department files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d24-f2" n="27" xml:id="d24-f2-content">
                <p>Brother of the Japanese Emperor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
